'''Lak Sivrak''' was a [[Shistavanen]] [[Gender|male]] who served the [[Galactic Empire]] as a [[scout]] and [[Hunting|hunter]]. He<ref name="FC" /> at one point was a patron of [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina]] in [[Mos Eisley]]<ref name="FansChoice">{{SWCT|set=Fans' Choice - 2022|cardname=Lak Sivrak}}</ref> [[spaceport]] on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]]<ref name="USW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> and left the establishment by a backdoor during a brawl.<ref name="FFG">{{FFGTCG|set=Desperate Circumstances|cardname=Lak Sivrak|link=alliances-cycle/desperate-circumstances/lak-sivrak-r2020}}</ref> After meeting the [[Force-sensitive]] [[Lamproid]] [[Dice Ibegon]],<ref name="FC" /> another patron of the [[cantina]],<ref name="Ibegon">{{ForceCollection|Dice Ibegon|star=1}}</ref> he fell in love with her.<ref name="FC" /> Ibegon was a member of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] and convinced Sivrak to join her cause<ref name="Ibegon" /> in the [[Galactic Civil War]] between the Empire and the rebels.<ref name="USW" />

In [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the [[Battle of Endor]] to [[4 ABY]].</ref> Sivrak [[Rebel Alliance Starfighter Corps|flew]] an [[X-wing starfighter]] for the rebels during the [[Battle of Endor]],<ref name="FC" /> in which the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Alliance Fleet]] engaged the [[Imperial Navy]] above the [[moon]] of [[Endor]] and successfully destroyed the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station|Death Star II]].<ref name="USW" /> Sivrak had [[Color|brown]] [[Hair|fur]], gray skin, and black [[eye]]s.<ref name="FFG" /> He wore a brown [[Clothing|shawl]] over a white shirt with a black [[belt]] and used a [[SE-14r light repeating blaster]].<ref name="GentleGiant">{{GentleGiantCite|set=Mini Busts|pack=Lak Sivrak|link=star-wars-a-new-hope-lak-sivrak-mini-bust}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
{{Listen3|Ibegon-Ketwol-Soundboard.flac||the audio of Dice Ibegon and Lak Sivrak that would be reused for Ibegon and Ketwol}}
Lak Sivrak was portrayed by [[Kim Falkinburg]]<ref name="Archeology">{{YouTube|video=ElyMaaAFLKU|text=The Star Wars Cantina PT. 2 &#124; Full Panel #indianacomicconvention #tomspinadesigns #starwarshistory|channel=@FanXComicConventions|name=FanX Comic Conventions|date=2025-05-03}}</ref> in the [[original trilogy]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']],<ref name="ANH">{{Film|IV}}</ref> which was released on [[May 25]], [[1977]].<ref name="YearByYear">''[[Star Wars Year By Year: A Visual History, New Edition]]''</ref> He was added to the film during<ref name="CantinaRollCall">{{SWArchive|url=episode-iv/bts/article/f20030502/index.html|text=Cantina Roll-Call: Shedding Light on Some Alien Aliases|int=Cantina Roll-Call: Shedding Light on Some Alien Aliases}}</ref> a series of supplemental shots filmed for the cantina sequence on a sound stage in Dovington's Hollywood studio between [[January 24]]&ndash;[[January 25|25]], 1977.<ref name="MakingOf">''[[The Making of Star Wars: The Definitive Story Behind the Original Film]]''</ref> Due to time and budget restraints,<ref name="Insider71">{{InsiderCite|71|Ask Lobot|Star Wars Q&A}}</ref> the Lak Sivrak mask was an off-the-shelf [[Wikipedia:Halloween|Halloween]] mask created by creature designer [[Rick Baker]], who also used an altered version of the same commercial mask for the cantina character [[Arleil Schous]]. Sivrak's shawl was a re-used [[Jawa]] robe.<ref name="YouTube">{{YouTube|video=d1AAd1tsPds|text=Star Wars: A New Hope &ndash; Cantina Archeology Part 2: Behind The Scenes of the Mos Eisley Cantina &ndash; US|channel=@CredibleNerds|name=The Credible Nerds}}</ref>

[[File:Sivrak-Mask.png|thumb|left|250px|Lak Sivrak used an off-the-shelf Halloween mask made by Rick Baker.]]
Sivrak's mask long bothered director [[George Lucas]],<ref name="CantinaRollCall" /> as although he had approved its use, the mask had been created outside his sphere of control.<ref name="Insider71" /> Because of this, he digitally replaced the character with the highly detailed puppet [[Ketwol]] in the ''[[The Star Wars Trilogy Special Edition|Special Edition]]'' version of ''A New Hope''<ref name="Ketwol">{{DB|character|ketwol|Ketwol}}</ref> released in [[1997]],<ref name="YearByYear" /> although the audio that was intended to be Sivrak growling was left unchanged.<ref name="BTM">''[[Star Wars: Behind the Magic]]''</ref>

Sivrak was known as "Hyena"<ref name="BTM" /> or "Hyena-Man" on set,<ref name="CantinaRollCall" /> but in the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], the character was first identified in the [[Star Wars video games|mobile card game]] ''[[Star Wars: Force Collection]]'',<ref name="FC" /> which initially launched in [[2013]]. Although the launch of ''Force Collection'' predates<ref name="Force Collection release">{{SW|url=news/announcing-star-wars-force-collection|text=Announcing Star Wars: Force Collection|nolive=1}}</ref> the ''Star Wars'' canon reset of [[2014]],<ref name="Legends">{{SW|url=news/the-legendary-star-wars-expanded-universe-turns-a-new-page|text=The Legendary Star Wars Expanded Universe Turns a New Page}}</ref> [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] member [[Leland Chee]] confirmed that the game was kept updated to fit with canon.<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|holocronkeeper|status/846807700482666496|[[Leland Chee]]|date=2017-03-28|quote=I'm not gonna go through the trouble of changing them and I don't have any reason to believe currently that anyone would. [&hellip;] On the off-chance that we DID have a current need to change any of these, we would have for Force Collection.|archivedate=20210505080831}} &mdash; [[Leland Chee]] of the [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] has confirmed that [[in-universe]] information from ''[[Star Wars: Force Collection]]'' conforms with ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]].</ref> The name originated in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, where [[Lak Sivrak/Legends|Sivrak]] was first identified in the [[1989]] ''[[Star Wars: The Roleplaying Game]]'' supplement ''[[Galaxy Guide 1: A New Hope]]'', which was written by [[Grant S. Boucher]] for [[West End Games]].<ref name="GG1">''[[Galaxy Guide 1: A New Hope]]''</ref> The [[Troig]]<ref name="AABR">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=16|story=All Aces Battle Royale (comic story)}}</ref> [[Jak Sivrak]], who was created for the [[2018]] animated television series ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'', was named as a reference to Lak Sivrak.<ref name="Syfy">{{WebCite|url=https://www.syfy.com/syfywire/star-wars-resistance-harbors-crazy-deep-cuts-and-will-cross-over-with-the-force-awakens|text=Star Wars Resistance harbors crazy deep cuts and will cross over with The Force Awakens|author=Young, Brian|date=2018-10-02|work=[[Wikipedia:Syfy|Syfy]]|archivedate=20191227161942}}</ref>

